# One more river - traditionele spiritual over de ark van Noach
# Traditioneel; bekend in veel varianten, vroege opnamen uit 1919 en 1935 (Traditional
# Ballad Index via folklorist.org). Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit ONE_MORE.RIV (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfouten hersteld: dubbel "The",
# "arive" werd "arrive", "het" werd "her". Het refrein staat in de bron eenmaal; hier na elk couplet herhaald.
# Akkoorden bij het refrein en het eerste couplet, naar de kolommen van de bron.
{title: One more river}
{meta: id one-more-river}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit ONE_MORE.RIV (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via folklorist.org (Traditional Ballad Index)}
{meta: tag geestelijk}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{key: F}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]One more [Bb]river [F]and that's the river of Jor[C7]dan[F]
One more [Bb]river, [F]there's one more [Bb]river to [C7]cross[F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Old [F]Noah once he build the Ark,
There's one more river to [C7]cross.[F]
And [F]patched it up with hickory bark
There's [C7]one more [F]river to cross.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: In de volgende coupletten volgt op elke regel de slotregel van het eerste couplet}

{start_of_verse}
He went to work to load his stock
He anchored the Ark with a great big rock
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in one by one
The elephant chewing a caraway bun
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in two by two
The rhinoceros and the kangaroo
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in three by three
The bear, the flea and the bumble bee
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in four by four
Old Noah got mad and hollered for more
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in five by five
with Saratoga trunks they did arrive
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in six by six
The hyena laughed at the monkey's tricks
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in seven by seven
Said the ant to the elephant, who are you a-shovin'
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in eight by eight
They came with a rush 'cause 'twas so late
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in nine by nine
Old Noah shouted, "Cut that line"
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The animals went in ten by ten
The Ark she blew her whistle then
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
And then the voyage did begin
Old Noah pulled the gang-plank in
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
They never knew where they were at
Till the old Ark bumped on Ararat
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
The old ark landed high and dry,
The baboon kissed the cow goodbye
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
